---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StatusTag from '../../components/StatusTag.astro';
import SourceLink from '../../components/SourceLink.astro';
import { discoverResult as result, artifactDigest, artifactUrl, sourceUrl } from '../../lib/modules';

const requestPath = 'conformance/discover_v1/fixtures/request.json';
const resultPath = 'conformance/discover_v1/fixtures/result.json';
const downloads = await Promise.all([requestPath, resultPath].map(async (path) => ({ path, digest: await artifactDigest(path) })));
---
<BaseLayout title="MathGraph Discover — Advisory attention, explicit boundaries" description="Inspect a real PARTIAL source-pack result from the local Discover contract, including incomplete replay material and exact provenance." currentPath="/discover/">
  <header class="section section--compact"><div class="shell">
    <div class="eyebrow">Discover · local advisory contract</div>
    <h1>Choose where to look next.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Discover ranks proposed continuations and allocates attention. The local deterministic contract preserves source gaps, reported observations, and the boundary between a candidate and an accepted claim.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href={artifactUrl(resultPath)}>Inspect the example result</a><a class="button button--secondary" href="/protocol/">Protocol and boundaries</a></div>
  </div></header>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell page-grid">
    <aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page"><strong>On this page</strong><a href="#example">Real example</a><a href="#missing">Replay boundary</a><a href="#sources">Source pins</a><a href="#contract">Local contract</a></aside>
    <div class="prose">
      <section id="example">
        <div class="eyebrow">Recursive residual transfer · 2026-05-23 source pack</div>
        <h2>An advisory result with missing material.</h2>
        <StatusTag label={result.status} tone="unknown" />
        <p>Verification status: <code>{result.verification_status}</code>. The adapter checked available source bytes and produced the committed ranking. The historical experiment was not rerun or requalified.</p>
        <p><code>advisory_only: {String(result.advisory_only)}</code><br /><code>can_promote_truth: {String(result.can_promote_truth)}</code></p>
        {result.ranked_candidates.map((candidate) => <div class="callout">
          <h3>Rank {candidate.rank}: <code>{candidate.candidate_id}</code></h3>
          <p>{candidate.suggested_route}</p>
          <p>Proposed target: <code>{candidate.descension_target}</code>. Selected: <code>{String(candidate.selected)}</code>.</p>
          <p>Attention allocation: <code>{candidate.attention_probability}</code>. Heuristic score: <code>{candidate.taste_score}</code>.</p>
        </div>)}
        <p><code>{result.attention_interpretation}</code>: attention is allocation, not truth confidence. A probability of 1 means all allocated attention goes to this one eligible candidate; it supplies no proof or truth score.</p>
        <details><summary>Reported historical metrics</summary><p>Reported historical metrics are source observations, not new verification results. Zero reported contamination and passed historical gates do not promote a claim.</p>
          <dl class="module-artifacts">{result.reported_metrics.map((metric) => <div><dt><code>{metric.name}</code></dt><dd>{String(metric.value)} · source <code>{metric.source_id}</code></dd></div>)}</dl>
        </details>
      </section>
      <section id="missing">
        <h2>Full replay remains unavailable.</h2>
        <p>The full candidate-score CSV and SQLite ledger are missing locally. The ledger is required for full replay; original equations, matrix, and toolchain qualification are not supplied by this adapter.</p>
        <p>Result reason: {result.reason_codes.map((reason) => <code>{reason}</code>)}</p>
        <details open><summary>Exact source diagnostics</summary><ul>{result.source_diagnostics.map((diagnostic) => <li><code>{diagnostic}</code></li>)}</ul></details>
      </section>
      <section id="sources">
        <h2>Inspect the source identities.</h2>
        <p>Digests establish byte identity relative to a trusted pin, not publisher authenticity. Missing artifacts retain their source references and <code>NOT_CHECKED</code> state.</p>
        <details><summary>All {result.sources.length} source references and digests</summary>
          <dl class="module-artifacts">{result.sources.map((source) => <div>
            <dt>{source.repo_path ? <a href={sourceUrl(source.repo_path)}>{source.source_id}</a> : <code>{source.source_id}</code>}</dt>
            <dd>{source.availability} · integrity {source.integrity_check} · {source.size_bytes} bytes<br /><code>{source.sha256}</code><br />Required for full replay: {String(source.required_for_full_replay)}</dd>
          </div>)}</dl>
        </details>
        <div class="source-stack">{downloads.map(({ path, digest }) => <SourceLink href={artifactUrl(path)} label={path === requestPath ? 'Exact request JSON' : 'Exact result JSON'} meta={`SHA-256 ${digest}`} />)}</div>
        <p><a href={sourceUrl(resultPath)}>Committed result and source revision ↗</a></p>
      </section>
      <section id="contract">
        <h2>Run locally with explicit inputs.</h2>
        <p>Hosted service: <code>NOT_DEPLOYED</code>. This page is a static projection. The CLI performs no solver call, route execution, or semantic verification.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><div class="code-label">From a repository checkout · Python standard library</div><pre><code>python -I -S scripts/mathgraph_discover_v1.py --request conformance/discover_v1/fixtures/request.json</code></pre></div>
        <p><a href="/schemas/discover-request-v1.schema.json">Request schema</a> · <a href="/schemas/discover-result-v1.schema.json">Result schema</a> · <a href={sourceUrl('docs/discover_contract_v1.md')}>Full contract</a></p>
        <p>Modules can be used separately. <a href="/develop/">Develop</a> and <a href="/capabilities/">Capabilities</a> expose different contracts; no autonomous loop or compulsory runtime sequence is provided.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
